A||||6||cscougar||Dual exhaust question||||5
Z||000000||cscougar||09-23-1999||02:08 PM||||Will the dual exhaust from a 6cyl (muffler and tailpipes) fit a Fiero 4 cyl?  I put a GT front and rear fascia on my 85 2m4 and want to add duals.  It looks like I could buy a muffler for the 6 cyl and use the tailpipe for the duals.<P>Thanks,<P>Ted ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-23-1999||02:22 PM||||the "dual" exhaust splits out both sides of the v6 muffler. Yes it fits the 4 tho you might need an adaptor... or a diferant pipe from the catalyst.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||09-23-1999||05:29 PM||||I did this swap on my 4 cyl fiero and everything fit perfect. You will need the hangers for the v6 pipe, but the holes are in the cradle for them to bolt in already.||||reg||14
Z||000003||PaUL||09-23-1999||09:22 PM||||Actually some SE models came this way, with 4 cyl. and dual exhaust.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||09-24-1999||09:34 AM||||The Indy Pace Cars came this way, too.  The exhaust note sounds pretty cool, too!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||09-24-1999||02:25 PM||||I got the idea to put the duals on my car after seeing a friends 86 aero coupe- it looks just like an 85 gt with the ground effects, just has the iron duck instead of a real motor.||||reg||6
Z||000006||batboy||09-24-1999||04:43 PM||||My 1987 SE Fiero 4 cylinder has the factory four tipped "dual" exhaust.||||reg||1
